  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    grid = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find all non-zero cells\n    cells = {}\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                cells[(r,c)] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    # Find the unique color (appears once)\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(cells.values())\n    unique_color = [c for c,n in counts.items() if n == 1][0]\n    other_color = [c for c,n in counts.items() if n != 1][0]\n    \n    # Find position of unique color\n    ur, uc = [(r,c) for (r,c),v in cells.items() if v == unique_color][0]\n    \n    # Find centroid of the shape to determine direction\n    all_pos = list(cells.keys())\n    avg_r = sum(r for r,c in all_pos) / len(all_pos)\n    avg_c = sum(c for r,c in all_pos) / len(all_pos)\n    \n    # Direction from unique cell toward center of shape\n    dr = avg_r - ur\n    dc = avg_c - uc\n    \n    # Normalize to unit direction\n    if abs(dr) > abs(dc):\n        dr = 1 if dr > 0 else -1\n        dc = 0\n    else:\n        dc = 1 if dc > 0 else -1\n        dr = 0\n    \n    # Draw line in opposite direction\n    nr, nc = ur - dr, uc - dc\n    while 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n        if grid[nr][nc] == 0:\n            grid[nr][nc] = unique_color\n        nr -= dr\n        nc -= dc\n    \n    return grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    grid = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find all non-zero cells\n    cells = {}\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                cells[(r,c)] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    # Find the unique color (appears once)\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(cells.values())\n    unique_color = [c for c,n in counts.items() if n == 1][0]\n    other_color = [c for c,n in counts.items() if n != 1][0]\n    \n    # Find position of unique color\n    ur, uc = [(r,c) for (r,c),v in cells.items() if v == unique_color][0]\n    \n    # Find centroid of the shape to determine direction\n    all_pos = list(cells.keys())\n    avg_r = sum(r for r,c in all_pos) / len(all_pos)\n    avg_c = sum(c for r,c in all_pos) / len(all_pos)\n    \n    # Direction from unique cell toward center of shape\n    dr = avg_r - ur\n    dc = avg_c - uc\n    \n    # Normalize to unit direction\n    if abs(dr) > abs(dc):\n        dr = 1 if dr > 0 else -1\n        dc = 0\n    else:\n        dc = 1 if dc > 0 else -1\n        dr = 0\n    \n    # Draw line in opposite direction\n    nr, nc = ur - dr, uc - dc\n    while 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n        if grid[nr][nc] == 0:\n            grid[nr][nc] = unique_color\n        nr -= dr\n        nc -= dc\n    \n    return grid",
